.TH SPRITERAW 1
.SH NAME
spriteraw \- a sprite built by hand, element by element
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spriteraw
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I SpriteRaw
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/SpriteRaw.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
"Normally, you make sprites with <CTRL-r>.  This shows how to build a
sprite by hand."  A green triangle with a flooded interior, assembled
from a colour element, three lines and a flood fill.  The element list is
printed under the drawing in the same vocabulary
.IR spriteedit (1)
edits, so the hand-built sprite can be read as well as drawn.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/spriteraw.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR spriteedit (1),
.IR wm (1)
